{
  "manufacturer": "Lumel",
  "manufacturer_slug": "lumel",
  "model": "ND20 network parameter meter",
  "model_slug": "nd20",
  "short_model": "ND20",
  "aliases": [
    "ND20",
    "ND20-xxxx"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Power meter (panel network parameter meter)",
  "applies_to": "Lumel ND20 panel meter per the ND20 user's manual; registers 4056-4061 need firmware 1.09 or later and are not listed here.",
  "summary": "The ND20 is a 96x96 panel meter for 3- and 1-phase networks with an RS-485 Modbus RTU port. Each measured value is offered as a float in several register areas; this map uses the 7000 area (two 16-bit registers per value, high word first) plus the 4000 area of 16-bit settings, 32-bit energy counters and the status word.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": 1,
    "baud": 9600,
    "parity": "None",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": 2,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "0-based",
    "note": "Addresses are used as printed: the manual's example frames read 4000 as 0x0FA0, 7000 as 0x1B58 and 7500 as 0x1D4C. For the float area the 'documented' field shows the table's '6xxx/7xxx' pair; this map uses the 7xxx address."
  },
  "default_word_order": "ABCD",
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "Meter of network parameters ND20 type - User's manual",
    "doc_number": null,
    "revision_date": null,
    "url": "https://asset.conrad.com/media10/add/160267/c1/-/en/001384097ML02/upute-za-rukovanje-1384097-lumel-nd20-221100m1.pdf",
    "unofficial": true,
    "pages": "Serial link and example frames pp. 37-40; register map overview p. 41; Table 11 (4000 area) pp. 43-47; status bits p. 48; Table 12 (float areas) pp. 51-54 (printed page numbers)"
  },
  "notes": [
    "Source is Conrad's copy of the unaltered Lumel manual; Lumel's own site did not turn up a public copy of the full manual in two searches, though its quick-start guides point to lumel.com.pl.",
    "Float areas: 7000-7319 is two 16-bit registers per value with bytes 3-2-1-0 (ABCD), confirmed by the example frame that returns 41 20 00 00 = 10.0. The 6000 area holds the same values with bytes 1-0-3-2 (CDAB) and 7500 the same values as single 32-bit registers; only the 7000 area is listed here.",
    "Energy in the 4000 area is (high register x 65536 + low register) / 10 in kWh or kvarh, per the manual's formulas.",
    "Left out: 7054 (labelled 'Mean Tg factor of phase L1', which does not fit a 3-phase mean), the min/max area from 7128 on, harmonic energy overflow pairs 7112-7118, time registers 7120-7124, the averaged power archive 1000-1077, alarm and analog output setup 4001-4002 and 4012-4029, display configuration 4054-4056, and 4057 (its value list prints 3Ph/4W twice).",
    "Which quantities are valid depends on the connection (3Ph/4W, 3Ph/3W, 1Ph/2W); Table 12 marks phase values that are not available in 3-wire mode."
  ],
